Upstream: none found.

CodebookBuilder::make returns an empty codebook for an empty code list, and read_codebook then
indexed its empty lookup table and panicked. Vorbis is the only decoder that builds codebooks from
stream data, and a sparse Vorbis codebook without used entries is empty. Without this patch and
fix-vorbis-codebook-lookup.patch, decode_any panics (index out of bounds in read_codebook) on an
Ogg Vorbis stream whose floor reads from such a codebook. fix-vorbis-codebook-lookup.patch, applied
earlier, rejects empty Vorbis codebooks during setup, so the harnesses do not reach this check
while it is applied.

